# Fixtures no test device can provide, written by hand after these formats:
#
# sys/class/hwmon/hwmon0, links.json
#   A Nuvoton NCT6779D Super-I/O as on x86 routers: temperatures with labels and
#   PWM outputs. Attribute names and units: the kernel's
#   Documentation/hwmon/sysfs-interface.rst; the chip name, temperature source
#   labels and platform device (nct6775.656): Documentation/hwmon/nct6775.rst
#   and drivers/hwmon/nct6775-core.c.
# sys/class/hwmon/hwmon1
#   A chip with neither a name file nor a device link, below 0 degrees.
# var/prometheus/*.prom
#   Files as node_exporter's textfile collector reads them: Prometheus text
#   exposition format 0.0.4 (prometheus.io/docs/instrumenting/exposition_formats);
#   truncated.prom is one whose writer died mid-line, which is why node_exporter
#   recommends writing to a temporary file and renaming it.
# sockets/unbound.stats_noreset.txt
#   Unbound 1.26.1's (OpenWrt 25.12's) reply to `UBCT1 stats_noreset` on its
#   control socket, what `unbound-control stats_noreset` prints: num-threads 2
#   (the UCI's num_threads), no dnscrypt and no extended-statistics (OpenWrt's
#   defaults). Lines and number formats: daemon/remote.c's do_stats(),
#   print_stats() and print_uptime(); the totals as daemon/stats.c's
#   server_stats_add() makes them (sums, the maximum for the .max counters,
#   the mean of the thread medians); the counters' meaning:
#   doc/unbound-control.rst, "Statistic Counters".
